## 5️⃣ Testing

### 5.1 Unit Tests (Jest + React Testing Library)

```tsx
// __tests__/ProductCard.test.tsx
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import { ProductCard } from '../components/ProductCard';

test('renders product card with title and price', () => {
  render(
    <ProductCard
      id="123"
      title="Test Product"
      price={19.99}
      imageUrl="/placeholder.png"
    />
  );

  expect(screen.getByText(/Test Product/i)).toBeInTheDocument();
  expect(screen.getByText(/\$19\.99/i)).toBeInTheDocument();
});
```

### 5.2 End‑to‑End Tests (Cypress)

```js
// cypress/integration/shop.spec.js
describe('Shop flow', () => {
  it('adds a product to cart and checks out', () => {
    cy.visit('/');
    cy.contains('Test Product').click();
    cy.get('[data-testid=add-to-cart]').click();
    cy.get('[data-testid=cart-count]').should('contain', '1');
    cy.get('[data-testid=checkout-button]').click();
    cy.get('[data-testid=card-element]').type('4242424242424242{enter}');
    cy.contains('Payment succeeded').should('be.visible');
  });
});
```

> **Tip:** Use Cypress’ `cy.intercept()` to mock API responses during tests.

---

## 6️⃣ Performance & SEO

| Tool | How to use |
|------|------------|
| **Next.js Image** | `<Image src="/img.jpg" width={500} height={300} />` automatically optimizes images. |
| **Static Generation** | `getStaticProps` + `getStaticPaths` for product pages. |
| **Incremental Static Regeneration** | `revalidate: 60` to refresh stale pages every minute. |
| **Code Splitting** | Dynamic imports: `const LazyComponent = dynamic(() => import('../components/Lazy'));` |
| **Lighthouse** | Run `npm run dev` → open Chrome DevTools → Lighthouse → generate report. |
| **SEO meta tags** | Use `next/head` to set `<title>`, `<meta name="description">`, `<link rel="canonical">`. |
| **Structured Data** | Add JSON‑LD script tags for products, breadcrumbs, reviews. |

---

## 7️⃣ Accessibility Checklist

| Check | Implementation |
|-------|----------------|
| **Semantic HTML** | Use `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<footer>`. |
| **ARIA labels** | `<button aria-label="Add to cart">` |
| **Keyboard navigation** | Ensure focus states, tab order, skip links. |
| **Color contrast** | Verify WCAG AA compliance (use Chrome Lighthouse). |
| **Alt text** | `<img alt="Product image">` |
| **Skip to content** | `<a href="#main" className="sr-only focus:not-sr-only">Skip to main content</a>` |

---

## 8️⃣ Deployment

| Platform | Steps |
|----------|-------|
| **Vercel** | `vercel login` → `vercel` → set env vars (`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`). |
| **Netlify** | Drag & drop repo → set build command `npm run build` → publish directory `out`. |
| **AWS Amplify** | Connect repo → auto‑build → set environment variables. |
| **Docker** | Build image: `docker build -t ecommerce-frontend .` → run: `docker run -p 3000:3000 ecommerce-frontend`. |

> **Tip:** Use a CDN (Cloudflare, Fastly) to cache static assets globally.

---

## 9️⃣ Continuous Integration / Delivery

```yaml
# .github/workflows/ci.yml
name: CI

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:

jobs:
  build-test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v3
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v3
        with:
          node-version: '20'
          cache: 'npm'
      - run: npm ci
      - run: npm run lint
      - run: npm run test
      - run: npm run build
```

Deploy to Vercel or Netlify automatically after successful build.

